-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock (Affliction): Improved Howl of Terror -> Fel Interdiction
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- TODO.md: "Improved Howl of Terror should be replaced by Fel Interdiction,
--           staggering 50% of damage taken when Fel Armor is being used.
--           Similar to the Ember Scar mechanic for Fire Mages we added, but
--           instead of clearing stacks with spell crits stacks are cleared
--           through casting drain soul, and stacks 10 times instead of 5.
--           It should also be moved to the slot to the right of Malediction."
--
-- Rename-in-place, per the house pattern (woa_2026_08_01_07.sql): talent 1668
-- keeps its ID and its rank-1 spell 30054; only the DBC row is rewritten.
-- Rank 2 (30057) is dropped -- the ability has no per-rank scaling, so this
-- becomes a 1-point talent like Sacrifice the Weak and Infernal Bargain.
--
-- The mechanic mirrors Ember Scars (MoltenArmor.cpp): a UnitScript::OnDamage
-- hook splits incoming damage and pushes the deferred half into a stacking
-- self-DoT, here Mark of Gul'dan (200520).  What differs is the clearing
-- path.  Ember Scars needs a three-hop 200041 -> 200040 -> AuraScript relay
-- because AzerothCore has no "on spell crit" hook; Drain Soul damage IS
-- reachable by an ordinary spell_proc, so Fel Interdiction's own aura is the
-- proc carrier and no relay spells exist.
--
-- Spells:
--   30054  = Fel Interdiction (talent aura; carries the stagger % AND the
--            Drain Soul proc)
--   200520 = Mark of Gul'dan (the deferred-damage DoT, 10 stacks / 10s)
-- Talent: 1668, Affliction (TabID 302), moved Tier 7 Col 0 -> Tier 7 Col 3.
-- ===========================================================================


-- ============================================================
-- Improved Howl of Terror -> Fel Interdiction (talent 1668, rank 1)
-- ============================================================
-- Effect 1 becomes SPELL_AURA_DUMMY: a marker aura the UnitScript checks for,
-- and whose amount IS the stagger percentage, so 50% lives in exactly one
-- place.  EffectDieSides1 stays 1, so CalcValue = BasePoints + 1 = 50 --
-- the value GetAmount() returns and the value $s1 renders.
--
-- The talent also carries the Drain Soul proc itself (spell_proc below), so
-- ProcFlags/ProcChance are set here to match the Syncretism precedent
-- (2026_03_30_02.sql) of declaring them in the DBC as well as the proc row.
--
-- EffectMiscValue1 10 (SPELLMOD_CASTING_TIME) and EffectSpellClassMaskA2 8
-- are Improved Howl of Terror leftovers and MUST be zeroed -- left in place
-- they would silently constrain the redesigned effect.
--
-- Both SpellDescription0 and SpellToolTip0 are set: the talent pane renders
-- the description, the buff bar renders the tooltip.
-- Generated by gen_sql.py on 2026-08-06
-- Overrides: SpellName0: 'Improved Howl of Terror' -> 'Fel Interdiction', SpellRank0: 'Rank 1' -> '', ProcFlags: 0 -> 327680, ProcChance: 101 -> 100, DurationIndex: 21 -> 21, Effect1: 6 -> 6, EffectApplyAuraName1: 107 -> 4, EffectBasePoints1: -801 -> 49, EffectDieSides1: 1 -> 1, EffectMiscValue1: 10 -> 0, EffectImplicitTargetA1: 1 -> 1, EffectSpellClassMaskA2: 8 -> 0, SpellIconID: 134 -> 2297, SpellDescription0: 'Reduces the casting time of your Howl of Terror spell by $/1000;S1 sec.' -> 'When using Fel Armor, $s1% of damage taken is converted to a Mark of Gul'dan, dealing damage periodically. Stacks can be removed by dealing damage with Drain Soul.', SpellToolTip0: '' -> 'When using Fel Armor, $s1% of damage taken is converted to a Mark of Gul'dan.'

