-- ============================================================
-- NEW spell 200520: Mark of Gul'dan (the deferred-damage DoT)
-- ============================================================
-- Cloned from Ember Scars (200023) so the DoT plumbing matches exactly:
-- SPELL_AURA_PERIODIC_DAMAGE on a 1000ms amplitude, DurationIndex 1 (10s).
-- Changes from the base: StackAmount 5 -> 10, school Fire -> Shadow, its own
-- icon, and no ProcFlags (Ember Scars' 65536 was never used).
--
-- AttributesEx3 67108864 = SPELL_ATTR3_SUPPRESS_CASTER_PROCS.  This is load-
-- bearing: without it the DoT's own Shadow ticks could proc the redesigned
-- Siphon Life (woa_2026_08_06_00.sql) and heal back the damage the talent
-- just deferred, cancelling the mechanic.  Same precedent as
-- SpellInfoCorrections.cpp:4805, which sets it on Siphon Life's heal.
--
-- EffectBasePoints1 -1 with DieSides 1 = 0 damage.  The real per-tick amount
-- is written by C++ at apply time via AuraEffect::ChangeAmount, which is why
-- the tooltip is prose rather than a $ variable -- a variable would render 0.
-- Generated by gen_sql.py on 2026-08-06
-- Overrides: SpellName0: 'Ember Scars' -> 'Mark of Gul'dan', SpellRank0: '' -> '', AttributesEx3: 0 -> 67108864, StackAmount: 5 -> 10, DurationIndex: 1 -> 1, ProcFlags: 65536 -> 0, ProcChance: 100 -> 0, Effect1: 6 -> 6, EffectApplyAuraName1: 3 -> 3, EffectAmplitude1: 1000 -> 1000, EffectBasePoints1: -1 -> -1, EffectDieSides1: 1 -> 1, EffectImplicitTargetA1: 6 -> 1, SchoolMask: 4 -> 32, SpellIconID: 1986 -> 3172, ActiveIconID: 1986 -> 3172, SpellVisual1: 46 -> 0, SpellFamilyName: 0 -> 0, SpellDescription0: '50% of damage taken while protected by Molten Armor is dealt over time. Each hit taken adds a stack, with each stack having an equal amount of damage. Spell critical hits clear a stack of Ember Scars. ' -> 'Damage deferred by Fel Interdiction, dealt over time. Each hit taken adds a stack. Dealing damage with Drain Soul clears a stack.', SpellToolTip0: 'Damage is being delayed by your Molten Armor.' -> 'Damage is being delayed by your Fel Armor.'

